From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wcn36xx: retain learned scan fallback across resume

The SM-T531 firmware capability exchange advertises scan offload again
when mac80211 restarts the device after suspend. This loses the existing
fallback decision, causing another ten-second channel-list timeout on
every resume and delaying Wi-Fi and SSH recovery.

Remember a failed offload request for the lifetime of the device and
clear the renewed offload capability before scanning. Continue using the
existing mac80211 software scan. Unbinding/reprobing resets this state;
no firmware version or board identifier is hard-coded.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/main.c
index aa8aaa2a6..a6a3e4e33 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/main.c
@@ -633,6 +633,10 @@ static int wcn36xx_hw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	struct wcn36xx *wcn = hw->priv;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* A firmware capability exchange on resume must not undo the fallback. */
+	if (wcn->scan_offload_failed)
+		wcn36xx_firmware_clear_feat_caps(wcn->fw_feat_caps, SCAN_OFFLOAD);
+
 	if (!wcn36xx_firmware_get_feat_caps(wcn->fw_feat_caps, SCAN_OFFLOAD)) {
 		/* fallback to mac80211 software scan */
 		return 1;
@@ -668,6 +672,7 @@ static int wcn36xx_hw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	wcn->scan_req = NULL;
 	mutex_unlock(&wcn->scan_lock);
 	wcn36xx_firmware_clear_feat_caps(wcn->fw_feat_caps, SCAN_OFFLOAD);
+	wcn->scan_offload_failed = true;
 	wcn36xx_warn("Firmware scan unavailable (%d), using software scan\n", ret);
 	return 1;
 }
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/wcn36xx.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/wcn36xx.h
index 8c43f67bd..3aa0b346c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/wcn36xx.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/wcn36xx.h
@@ -265,6 +265,7 @@ struct wcn36xx {
 	struct ieee80211_vif	*sw_scan_vif;
 	struct mutex		scan_lock;
 	bool			scan_aborted;
+	bool			scan_offload_failed;
 
 	/* DXE channels */
 	struct wcn36xx_dxe_ch	dxe_tx_l_ch;	/* TX low */
